{"availability":"available","full":"DrumScript/DrumScript","name":"DrumScript","description":"DrumScript is an open-source Python library and suite of tools for drummers","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":61,"forks":5,"created":"2025-06-17T15:45:44Z","updated":"2026-10-09T02:39:51Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://drumscript.github.io/DrumScript/","topics":["audio","drums","music","python"],"demo":"https://drumscript.github.io/DrumScript/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:57.015Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:57.015Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:57.015Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:57.015Z","stars":61,"forks":5}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["DrumScript is an open-source Python library and CLI tool for drum audio analysis and automatic drum transcription. It also serves as a wrapper for extracting drums from songs using Demucs and creating drumless backing tracks from any song.","By default DrumScript accepts drum- and percussion-only audio (.wav or .mp3). If you specify the --full-song flag when using transcribe() it will first extract the drums from song using Demucs 4-part model and then transcribe.","DrumScript (both the Python package and the eventual UI) aims to be a free-to-use, open-source, zero-egress tool that allows you to give it a recording - a full mix or an isolated drum stem - and it will generate PDF sheet music, MIDI files, and MusicXML output."],"features":["Known dependency warnings","Automatic Drum Transcription: Detects kicks, snares, hi-hats, toms, and cymbals using a deterministic, rule-based classification engine - no machine learning required.","Tempo Detection: Automatically estimates BPM using a voting-system algorithm tuned for percussive audio.","Onset Detection: Onset detection method tuned to the physics of percussion audio rather than polyphonic instruments (piano, guitar, etc.).","Stem Separation: Uses the state-of-the-art Demucs source separation model to isolate drums, bass, vocals, and other instruments from a full mix."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/DrumScript/DrumScript/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"6f2f099adf6681e96d3b423784ff61ccbb6e149882923bfb6bb016fa9b9fe7fd","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:57.369Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:57.369Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"DrumScript is an open-source Python library and CLI tool for drum audio analysis and automatic drum transcription. It also serves as a wrapper for extracting drums from songs using Demucs and creating drumless backing tracks from any song.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/DrumScript/DrumScript/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"6f2f099adf6681e96d3b423784ff61ccbb6e149882923bfb6bb016fa9b9fe7fd","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/DrumScript/DrumScript/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:57.370Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T02:39:51Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/DrumScript/DrumScript/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:57.371Z","hash":"6f2f099adf6681e96d3b423784ff61ccbb6e149882923bfb6bb016fa9b9fe7fd","originalBytes":29293,"storedBytes":29293,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["drumscript","audio","drum","full","python","pdf","install","model","stem","transcription","benchmarks","classification","pull","back","drums","midi","output","result","song","using","mp3","print","import","what","demucs","extract","ffmpeg","path","run","transcribe","zsh","code","data","deterministic","dev","docs","drumless","git","detection","engine","learning","librosa","onset","package","pydub","request","score","stems","tempo","uses","via","when","which","any","audio.wav","backing","dataset","datasets","dependencies","does","eval","extra","files","freq","idmt","license","machine","max","min","mir","note","please","accuracy","analysis","api",